ted on that breadboard  system was presented at the podium  at asms 2018 by huizeng  in january 2019 lab site was acquired  by beckmann culture life sciences and  opco  of danaher corporation the following  asms  in 2019 psyx pre-announced  the commercial release of the echo ms  and we eagerly anticipate  the official commercial release uh any  week now  mid-2020  here's what the breadboard system looks  like these are installed at merck and  plyser  you're looking at a 3d four poly for a  source plate mounted to an xy  stage you can see the open port  interface with two lines coming in one  for the carrier solvent  and one the capillary carrier the mix of  solvent  and sample for electrospray ionization  that's in the top  panel in the lower left we have the  acoustic transducer in a black housing  there's coupling fluid to connect the  transducer to  the bottom of the source plate for a  continuous fluid path  in the lower right we have the opi  housing and you can see  the gap between the housing and the  capillary that's where the sheath  carrier solvent flow occurs and then you  can see the  inner diameter of the capillary where  the vortex forms due to capillary  aspiration  in operation there's a video  to be shown here we're going to  highlight the  coverage the performance of this system  as conventional electrospray ionization  with wide and light coverage  this is an intact antibody standard at  150 kilodaltons  we're looking at two different  concentrations 10x difference limit of  detection is less than one  femtomole loading in the lower right  we have a choline transporter assay  where once again  we're demonstrating concordance with  lcms  over a range of inhibitor and stimulator  compounds with good agreement  [Music]  on the top left is a set of  plasma samples ranging from protein  precipitated  through neat plasma we're looking at  triplicate sets of peaks the analyte is  verapamil and what you notice is as we  go from protein precipitated  through 50 50 plasma water some with  formic acid all the way to neat plasma  we get a consistent set of peaks  we see slightly lower peaks or neat  plasma  due to some iron suppression but we have  sufficient signal  nevertheless to generate a standard  curve in all four cases  in the top right we have two peptides at  three different concentrations  looking at the effect of surfactant a  potent ion suppressor  so in the lower rate you can see with  and without  0.01 percent between 20 no ion  suppression  is observed  the next example is a demonstration of  real-time kinetics monitoring  we're looking at a sip 2d6 enzymatic  reaction  showing substrate dxm converted to  metabolite dxo that's dextromethorphan  over a 30 minute time course you can see  the intensity of  dxm decline as the product dxo  increases at each time point we have a  measurement  of six concentrations in duplicate we  get a linear response  the peak area over time at each  concentration  increases linearly with a good linear  fit good r squared  and we can analyze that with a  michaelis-menten  fit to the formation rate for metabolism  of dxm  to dxo by sip2d6 in human liver  microsomes  yielding a km 3.79 in agreement with  reported values  now we want to address fluorescent probe  artifacts  here we have an acyl transferase  activity assay  looking at glycerol 3-phosphate  in combination with a cofactor acyl coa  and the acyl transferase enzyme  converting to  phosphatic acid you want to look at  panel c and f initially so here we're  going  uh looking at the the relevance the  importance of the presence of both  acyl transferees and cofactor product is  only produced  when we have both the enzyme and the  cofactor  present moving to panel e we're sweeping  from low to high  the concentration of the cofactor acyl  coa and you can see there is a peak  going to the lower panel g looking at  the one micromolar  point you can see discrepancy in the  dotted line which is the ecoms data  and the fluor